title: Undo and restart
intro: Grid puzzles with no code: Z takes a move back, R starts the level over, and a counter shows the moves.

project: Empty | Crate Undo

chapter: A puzzle to get wrong | A goal brings a Move History along
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 11111111\n1......1\n1......1\n1......1\n11111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
look: 4, -2.5, 4
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position.X = 1.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
deselect
create: Crate
set: Transform.Position.X = 3.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
deselect
create: Goal
set: Transform.Position.X = 5.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
say: A room, a grid player, a crate, and a goal to push it onto.
expectcomponents: Goal = Transform, Sprite, Goal, MoveHistory
explain: component:MoveHistory | Move History | The first goal in a scene brings a Move History along. Every step the player takes, with any crate it pushes, is a move it can take back.
explain: field:MoveHistory.UndoAction | Undo | Undo is Z, U or the left shoulder button, and holding it keeps going back.
explain: field:MoveHistory.RestartAction | Restart | Restart is R or the left trigger. It puts everything back where the level started, and Undo can take that back too.
explain: field:MoveHistory.RestartReloads | Restart Reloads | Or tick this to reload the whole scene instead, so pickups and scripts start over as well.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Moves
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = TopLeft
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 2.5, -0.7
add: Counter
set: Counter.Track = *
set: Counter.Output = Moves
set: Counter.Format = Moves: {0}
explain: field:Counter.Output | Moves | A counter can count the moves, an output of the move history, going back down with each undo.

chapter: Take it back | Undo a mistake, restart, and undo the restart
play
wait: 0.5
tap: Down
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
expectat: Crate = 4.5, -2.5
say: Round behind the crate, and one push towards the goal.
tap: Up
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Down
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate = 4.5, -3.5
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves: 6
explain: game | Stuck | Oops. Pushed down against the wall, the crate can never get back up to the goal.
tap: Z
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate = 4.5, -2.5
expectat: Player = 4.5, -1.5
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves: 5
explain: game | Undo | Z takes the last move back. The crate and the player go back to where they were, and the count goes down.
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Down
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate = 5.5, -2.5
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves: 8
say: This time from the left, and it's home in eight moves.
tap: R
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate = 3.5, -2.5
expectat: Player = 1.5, -1.5
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves: 0
explain: game | Restart | R starts the level over: everything back where it began, and no moves taken.
tap: Z
wait: 0.5
expectat: Crate = 5.5, -2.5
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves: 8
explain: game | Undo the restart | And a restart is a move too, so Z brings the solved puzzle straight back.
stop
say: That's undo and restart for grid puzzles, with no code. Scripts can undo, restart and count moves of their own too.
